1. Balanced Brackets Checker
Detailed Scenario
A compiler assistant must quickly verify whether every opening bracket in a student program is closed in the correct order.
Detailed Description
Given a string containing only brackets (), {}, and [], determine whether the string is balanced. A string is balanced when 
each opening bracket has the same type of closing bracket and brackets close in the correct order.
Input Format
A single string S containing bracket characters.
Output Format
Print YES if the bracket string is balanced, otherwise print NO.
Constraints


1 <= |S| <= 100000
S contains only characters from: ( ) { } [ ]
Sample Input
{[()]}
Sample Output
YES
Explanation
Push opening brackets into a stack. When a closing bracket appears, the top of the stack must contain its matching opening 
bracket. At the end, the stack must be empty.
Array Implimentation:
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{ 
    char arr[100];
    scanf(" %[^\n]",arr);
    char stack[100];
    int top=-1;
    for(int i=0;arr[i]!='\0';i++){
        if(arr[i]=='(' || arr[i]=='[' || arr[i]=='{' ){
            stack[++top]=arr[i];
        }
        else if(top!=-1){
            if(arr[i]=='}' && stack[top]!='{'){printf("Invalid");return 0;}
             if(arr[i]==')' && stack[top]!='('){printf("Invalid");return 0;}
              if(arr[i]==']' && stack[top]!='['){printf("Invalid");return 0;}
            top--;
        }
        else{
            printf("Invalid");
            return 0;
        }
    }
if(top!=-1)printf("Invalid");
else{
printf("Valid");
    }
    return 0;
}
